abstract: >-
  Research software implementing the decision-support layer of "Evidence-Aware Multisensor Monitoring
  for Critical Infrastructure Incident Support" (Torstensson et al., 2026). An agent ingests a
  multisensor incident dataset, applies coverage-aware physiological rules (Eq. 1-5) and a
  source-qualified zone incident state (Eq. 6-7), and plans rescue logistics (personnel accounting,
  exact lexicographic team-task assignment, Eq. 8-9) and consequence-liquidation logistics (exact
  service-continuity allocation, Eq. 10-11, and a resource-constrained recovery schedule). All plans
  are deterministic proposals requiring human authorisation by the roles of Table 9, recorded in a
  hash-chained audit log. An optional language-model layer only summarises minimised aggregates.
  Reproduces Table 10 and Section 4.9 exactly. Not validated against real rescue operations.
keywords:
